.TH PLANET 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
planet \- Claim a world region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B planet
.I world
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Claim world
.I world
(0\-65535) as a region, and report it back as a region header giving its id,
width, world number, owner, and loaded module count. The world is yours from
then on: its rooms fall under your rule, and region\-scoped commands take it
as a selector.
.PP
Carving a new world out of the cosmos is a cosmos\-level decision, so only
the cosmos ruler may claim a world nobody holds. Taking back your own world,
or one nobody holds that was claimed before, needs no further leave. A world
already claimed by someone else answers with its owner's name.
.PP
A reclaim keeps the world's module set: the new ruler inherits the planet's
code and unloads what they do not want. Note that \fBroom\fP never claims:
carved rooms sit in whatever region covers them until this command claims
their world.
.PP
This command claims one world for yourself. To attribute any region \-\- a
district, a super\-planet region, or a world for someone else \-\- see
\fBgrant\fP(10).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR planets,here,release,grant,room,modlist (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
